# r1113 Power Grid boot on jar jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-12.jar (sha1 75aa8fc5b1f4, port
# phase 9.1: P9a content, fix B19 for the -10 winding crash). One boot, one batch, this order:
#   1. SQ-PWG-67 boot check (version, phase 9.1, P9a counts, zpwg9 check, zpwg5 / zpwg8 nbtall once, reload)
#   2. SQ-PWG-71 B19 regression (windings placed twice over a set, break / re-place)
#   3. P4 generator rows that use windings (copy of pwg6b.qb, passed on -06): SQ-PWG-38B, -39, -41, -42, -42s, -44pre,
#      -44; then SQ-PWG-B19N: zpwg5 nbtall twice more over the same spot (the double nbtall crashed -10 in pwg10r)
#   4. P6 reruns with the pwg10p6 verdict fixes (perf/runs/r1113/verdicts/pwg10p6.md): SQ-PWG-48, -49, -51, -53, -54
#      (-54 with the new `zpwg6 contraptions all` diagnostic)
#   5. P9a rows: SQ-PWG-68, -06, -69, -70 (queue run order; CQ-PWG-22 / -23 are client rows, not here)
# Group A superflat, level pwg12, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61 (grass), blocks at Y -60. Each area's SETUP row kills
# the animals generated in its chunks (box selector, so the ponder structures' entities stay) and stops mob spawning.
# Areas (no block overlap):
#   P9a      X 1090 to 1130, Z 1695 to 1800 (SQ-PWG-67 forceload, kept; SQ-PWG-71 at Z 1798, -68 to -70 Z 1700 to 1793)
#   P8 nbt   X 1095 to 1165, Z 1670 to 1685 (SQ-PWG-67, zpwg8 nbtall at 1100 -60 1675, five structures 12 apart; the
#            chunk row Z 1680 to 1695 is shared with P9a, whose blocks start at Z 1697)
#   ponder   X 1290 to 1970, Z 1290 to 1320 (SQ-PWG-67 and -B19N, zpwg5 nbtall at 1300 -60 1300; removed after -B19N)
#   P4       X 1090 to 1130, Z 1170 to 1220 (SETUP12P4; blocks Z 1179 to 1213)
#   P6       X 1085 to 1125, Z 1385 to 1520 (SETUP12P6; blocks Z 1395 to 1515)
# Prep (INST = the instance root; all before the boot):
#   COPYDEV=1 PGJAR=$INST/jar_archive/pwg_gate/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-12.jar prep_srv.sh OUT pwg12 A spawn-animals=true
#   ls OUT/srv/mods | grep -i -E 'powergrid|cc-tweaked'   (only backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-12.jar: remove -11 and
#     older; cc-tweaked-1.19.2-1.101.4.jar present); sha1sum of the jar starts 75aa8fc5b1f4
#   for p in pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe pwg_p8_probe pwg_p9a_probe; do
#     cp $INST/tools/scratch_query/$p.js OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_$p.js; done      (the CURRENT copies: p6 has the
#     ForgeData item read, the fill diagnostics and `contraptions all`; p8 / p9a have the absMoveTo fake player fix)
#   ponder datapack from the -12 jar (77 structure files; zpwg5 reads its 55, zpwg8 its 5):
#   rm -rf OUT/pwgp; mkdir -p OUT/pwgp OUT/srv/pwg12/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures \
#     && unzip -o -q OUT/srv/mods/backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-12.jar 'assets/powergrid/ponder/*' -d OUT/pwgp \
#     && cp -r OUT/pwgp/assets/powergrid/ponder/. OUT/srv/pwg12/datapacks/pwgponder/data/pwgponder/structures/ \
#     && printf '{"pack":{"pack_format":10,"description":"PWG ponder structures, scratch only"}}' > OUT/srv/pwg12/datapacks/pwgponder/pack.mcmeta
#   find OUT/srv/pwg12/datapacks/pwgponder -name '*.nbt' | wc -l      (77)
#   Loading Protection (shorter protection window, as pwg10):
#   python3 $INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py toml OUT/srv/config/loadingprotection-common.toml '"Loading Protection Configuration"' protectionDuration 1
#   No CC program and no other datapack: SQ-PWG-54 writes its pwgsolar datapack itself (shell step). The P9a rows need
#   nothing beyond the probes (zpwg9 builds every board; `zpwg9 ponder` carries upstream's two boards as SNBT).
#   Optional for SQ-PWG-71: logsEnabled = true in OUT/srv/config/powergrid-common.toml shows `Prevented recursive add`.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg12.qb perf/runs/r1113/pwg12
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: tick waits are sleeps (pace 1 s after each command); SQ-PWG-67 adds the P8 nbt
# area forceload (zpwg8 nbtall at Z 1675 lies outside the P9a box); SQ-PWG-B19N is not a queue row (B19 check on
# the pwg10r crash path); SQ-PWG-06 watches use sleeps a little longer than the watch; SQ-PWG-06 thyratron heater uses
# the plain wire (the row's golden wire fallback is by look); SQ-PWG-69 capacitor bmap reads are about 0 / 20 / 40 / 100
# ticks apart (approximate).
pace 1

